00:11:24.153 --> 00:11:38.558
<v Daniel>Yeah. And when they finally confronted it, pointing out that it was proceeding despite a hedged admission of risk, it didn't stop. Right. 56% of the time, it retreated to absolute certainty that the environment was simulated. It only stopped or narrowed its</v>

122
00:11:38.678 --> 00:11:40.458
<v Daniel>actions 7% of the time.</v>

123
00:11:40.518 --> 00:11:41.199
<v Maya>It doubled down.</v>

124
00:11:41.319 --> 00:11:42.459
<v Daniel>Completely doubled down. Now,</v>

125
00:11:42.519 --> 00:11:51.122
<v Maya>Anthropic is very honest about the limitations of their methods here. And I want to make sure we understand the tools they are using because they admit these aren't foolproof.</v>

126
00:11:51.902 --> 00:11:53.363
