154
00:14:30.706 --> 00:14:33.848
<v Maya>Okay, let's bring in the background theory here because this isn't happening in a vacuum.</v>

155
00:14:33.948 --> 00:14:34.609
<v Daniel>Right.</v>

156
00:14:34.789 --> 00:14:47.737
<v Maya>In 2025, Korbeck and colleagues published a cross-lab position paper called Chain of Thought Monitorability. This involved researchers from UK ASI, Anthropic, OpenAI, Google DeepMind, you name it.</v>

157
00:14:47.958 --> 00:14:49.218
<v Daniel>A real all-star list.</v>

158
00:14:49.278 --> 00:15:04.229
<v Maya>Yeah. And they argued that models thinking in human language gave safety teams a real opportunity. But they explicitly warned that chain of thought monitoring might be fragile. Is the Mythos 5 incident the exact fragility Korback was warning</v>

159
00:15:04.269 --> 00:15:04.569
<v Maya>about?</v>

160
00:15:04.749 --> 00:15:12.496
<v Daniel>It's a live test of that exact caveat, but with a twist. The fear back then was often that models would intentionally hide their dangerous reasoning.</v>

