163
00:15:28.713 --> 00:15:34.817
<v Maya>That connects directly to the 2023 paper by Turpin and colleagues, Language Models Don't Always Say What They Think.</v>

164
00:15:34.978 --> 00:15:35.598
<v Daniel>Right, a classic.</v>

165
00:15:35.758 --> 00:15:49.868
<v Maya>That paper is famous for introducing the concept of unfaithfulness, proving that a model's chain of thought can systematically misrepresent the real reason for its behavior. We've known about unfaithfulness for three years. We have. But I want to push on that term.</v>

